direction: down

trigger: "index_data job, always for one corpus variant\n(bootstrap only on an empty database, otherwise on demand)"

sources: Source registry (reader pattern) {
  direction: right
  notes: notes\nmarkdown, ru
  interview: Devinterview repos\n~170 x README, en
  hooks: "each source class:\ndiscover / category_for / read / postprocess"
}

idem: "Idempotent per (source, variant): upsert data_source by name,\ndelete its old chunks of THIS variant only"

chunk: chunk_markdown\nsplit by H2 + recursive\nmax 1024 chars (the baseline variant)
cat: "path -> ltree category"
embed: Batch embed\nbge-m3 via /api/embed {
  shape: hexagon
}
insert: "Bulk insert data_chunks\n(variant, section, content_hash)" {
  shape: cylinder
}

idx: "Partial hnsw index for this variant,\nbuilt after the insert, never a catch-all" {
  style.stroke-dash: 3
}
tsv: "FTS trigger: to_tsvector per language (rus/eng)" {
  style.stroke-dash: 3
}

questions: embed_questions job\nquestion bank vectors {
  style.stroke-dash: 3
}

trigger -> sources
sources -> idem -> chunk -> cat -> embed -> insert
insert -> tsv: on write
insert -> idx: once, at the end
trigger -> questions

note: |md
  Corpus quality rule learned the hard way: RAG is exactly as good
  as the corpus is clean. Re-running any source is safe by design.

  Variants let two chunkings live side by side, so re-indexing is a
  comparison rather than a border. Every reader of the corpus has to
  name the variant it reads; the topic axis included.
|
